{{Short description|Major drainage basin in Abyala}}
The '''Marañón basin''' is the part of [[Abyala]] drained by the [[Marañón River]] and its [[w:tributary|tributaries]], situated primarily within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. The basin is bounded to the north and east by the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]], to the south by the [[Galibi Highlands]] and the west by the [[Salsipuedes Sea]]. The basin covers more than {{Convert|8000000|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}} and lies mostly in [[Pindorama]] and the [[Bayara|Bayaran]] community. Almost all rivers to the west of the Matarrañya drain westward through the basin, which have collectively formed the [[Marañón Delta]]. Most of the delta is composed of {{W|alluvial}} soils made up by small sediment particles that finally settle down as river currents slow down in the estuary.

Most of the basin is covered by the [[Marañón rainforest]], also known as ''Maranyon''. With a {{Convert|6,000,000|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}} area of dense [[W:Temperate rainforest|temperate rainforest]], it is the largest rainforest in the world.  

